{#- The brand block: the seal, the site name, and the headline and description from the
    language's site text, headline.md and description.md, each shown only when the site
    has written it. The headline and description are plain text, not headings: the page's
    single H1 belongs to the page.
    The seal and the site name are separate links to the home page. The site name is the
    one everyone reaches, by Tab and by screen reader. The seal is a second, larger target
    for pointer and touch: it is out of the Tab order and hidden from screen readers, so
    the home page is reached once. Until a site chooses its own seal, it is the theme's
    placeholder mark. #}
{%- set headline = katagami.siteText[lang].headline %}
{%- set tagline = katagami.siteText[lang].description %}
<div class="brand">
  <a class="brand__seal" href="/{{ lang }}/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><span class="brand__mark"></span></a>
  <a class="brand__name" href="/{{ lang }}/" rel="home"><bdi>{{ site.name }}</bdi></a>
  {%- if headline.html %}
  <div class="brand__headline">{{ headline.html | safe }}</div>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if tagline.html %}
  <div class="brand__description">{{ tagline.html | safe }}</div>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
